# Recordings are byte exact: their SHA-256 is recorded in run files and pinned
# in tests, so git must never rewrite their line endings. Everything else that
# is text is checked out with LF on every platform, so prettier, the guards,
# and the tests see the same bytes on Windows as on Linux and macOS.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.jsonl -text
*.png binary
*.crt -text
*.private-key -text
